---
date: 2026-06-05T16:40:21-04:00
---

Wrenford is a small city on the edge of the [[Verdant Expanse]]. It was built by a number of [[Org/index|Orgs]] out of [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]] who wanted to log the copious timber in the Expanse, but the forest fought back until it was deemed too expensive to pursue. Now the city remains half-developed, never quite reaching the potential the Orgs originally saw but not dying out either.

Many of the residents of Wrenford are followers of the [[Green Father]] on top of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]].

Wrenford holds about two thousand people, which is not enough to legally make it a town. It was planned for far more. Office buildings stand where there is little business to fill them, and the train station has about eight tracks though it sees one train a day, maybe two. A tired conductor hands arriving passengers illustrated pamphlets of the city as it was meant to be. Most people dress in work suits and dresses. There is no public transport; the city never grew enough to need it. Wrenford has a motel and a pub where the house beer ferments with a strange herbaceous note.

There is one route out by rail, to [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], a day and a half away through the mountains. [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] runs it, and would rather push the train to a dangerous speed than arrive late.

On the city's outskirts, between the streets and the forest, sits the [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford Commune|Wrenford commune]].
